Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings > Usage counts them.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom by themselves: a plain dark wall with the CarmaCars logo, a dark glossy floor with the car''s reflection and a soft shadow under the tyres. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name on the wall behind the car. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with **Publish shifts**; jobs are given by themselves only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. You can give a job to a field person or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">On each public photo press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>. The editor opens.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The box over the plate is already suggested: as soon as the review opens, every outside photo (the More outside photos included) gets its suggestion, and those photos show Box suggested. Check it. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom by themselves: a plain dark wall with the CarmaCars logo, a dark glossy floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a soft shadow under the tyres. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name on the wall behind the car. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>; jobs are given by themselves only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. You can give a job to a field person or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-service', 'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.
2. Cars and terms: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
3. **Onboarding photos**: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender''s permission of each car. **Replace**, **Remove** (with a reason), **Approve** or **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.
4. **Government forms**: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. **Make again** makes a car''s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. Open a form and press **Change a value** to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under **Versions**, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. **Back to the records** puts a box''s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same.
5. **Add cars from a list of VINs**: paste or upload the VINs, **Preview**, then **Add**; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.
6. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
7. Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.
8. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

A car''s page has the same Government forms box (Owner & documents).

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, **Withdraw it** if needed.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press **Record an official form signed in ink**, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Waiting to sign** (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars'' witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.
