  '<p class="gd-p">Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.</p><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-inbox" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The inbox</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> tab, and press <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo&#39;s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write a text and press <b class="gd-ui">Send text</b>: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a reply</b> puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Stop texts</b> stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unknown-callers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unknown callers</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Unknown callers</b>. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b>, or find the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">Link to</b> the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. <b class="gd-ui">Match automatically again</b> undoes a link made by hand.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-missed-calls" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missed calls</h2><p class="gd-p">A missed call raises the task &quot;Missed call from ...&quot; for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, &quot;Missed call: text the caller back&quot;), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo&#39;s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-and-texts-on-records" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls and texts on records</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s Messages &amp; history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips <b class="gd-ui">Texts</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b>); an owner&#39;s page has &quot;Calls and texts&quot;. Calls are not recorded on the line for now, so there is no transcript or recording to show.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-activity-log-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Activity log (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section have one <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking&#39;s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">All</b> shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press <b class="gd-ui">All</b> to go back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type in <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> to find a word in the log; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it away.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">50 lines show at a time: <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> shows the next 50, <b class="gd-ui">Newest</b> goes back to the top.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b>, a text or call from them <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, a chat line <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> is above the log; the note shows in it at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking&#39;s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-quo-contacts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quo contacts</h2><p class="gd-p">Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site&#39;s version is sent again.</li><li>One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.</li><li>A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.</li><li>If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Quo contacts</b>: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and <b class="gd-ui">Sync everyone again</b>. Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;, turn it off.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-booking-texts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking texts</h2><p class="gd-p">Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;: the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>; press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-carmacars-app-links" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The CarmaCars app links</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder&#39;s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, <b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter page has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal&#39;s renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-call-button-through-twilio-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call button through Twilio (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Quo keeps incoming calls, texts and AI answering. <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a staff page rings the staff member&#39;s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo and says why.</p><p class="gd-p">Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, <b class="gd-ui">Reveal</b> shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'leads-and-sales-claims', 'chapter', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', null, 'Leads and Sales claims', 'Every lead in one place, claims, outcomes and the Sales team''s numbers.',
  'Every lead in one place: people who are not renters or owners yet, from every source, with who is working on each one. Open **People** > **Renters** > **All leads**. An alert for a new lead (in the app, on the phone, or by email) opens that lead''s own page.

## What is in the list

- **Renter leads**: the contact form, live chat, the phone number box, discount game claims, offers that expired, booking requests typed and not sent, calls missed from a number with no booking (they arrive by themselves within 15 minutes), and Live visitors who turned Hot and left an email.
- **Owner leads**: owner program enquiries, owner applications started and not finished, owner form contacts and earnings calculator contacts. They are also under **People** > **Owners** > **Leads**, and each New owner program enquiry task opens its lead.
- **Partner leads**: fleet suppliers, dealers, rental businesses and insurers.

Each card shows the name, phone, email, the source in plain words (a live chat lead says Live chat), how old it is, and the start of what they wrote. New and hot leads come first. Open a lead for everything they wrote, the live chat transcript, their calls, every contact logged and the claim history.

## Work a lead

1. Press **Claim** on a card, or **Next lead** for the oldest hot lead nobody holds. It is yours for 15 minutes; nobody else can work on it meanwhile.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**. Your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged on the lead. Each call, text, email or **Note** adds another 15 minutes to your claim, up to 60 minutes from when you claimed it.
3. Press **Outcome** and choose Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won (with the booking number when there is one) or Lost (say why). Won and lost close the lead.
4. Nothing more to do? Press **Mark handled**. Done with it for now? Press **Unclaim**: it goes back to the pool at once.

A claim that runs out returns the lead to the pool for everyone. One person holds at most 25 leads at a time. When a renter lead''s person books and the booking is confirmed, the lead closes as Won by itself, for the Sales person on the booking.

## As an Admin

- **Reassign** gives a lead to a person (their claim, and the lead is assigned to them). **Release** ends someone''s claim.
- **Sales team** shows each person''s leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week or this month, best first.
- **Settings** > **Sales** sets how long a claim holds for renter, owner and partner leads (10 to 15 minutes suggested), the most a claim can be extended to, how many leads one person may hold, and how long a lead counts as hot.

> Good to know: Filters narrow the list by type, source, status, age, person and your own leads; the search finds a name, phone number, email or words they wrote.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every lead in one place: people who are not renters or owners yet, from every source, with who is working on each one. Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b>. An alert for a new lead (in the app, on the phone, or by email) opens that lead&#39;s own page.</p><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-what-is-in-the-list" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What is in the list</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>: the contact form, live chat, the phone number box, discount game claims, offers that expired, booking requests typed and not sent, calls missed from a number with no booking (they arrive by themselves within 15 minutes), and Live visitors who turned Hot and left an email.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>: owner program enquiries, owner applications started and not finished, owner form contacts and earnings calculator contacts. They are also under <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, and each New owner program enquiry task opens its lead.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Partner leads</b>: fleet suppliers, dealers, rental businesses and insurers.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Each card shows the name, phone, email, the source in plain words (a live chat lead says Live chat), how old it is, and the start of what they wrote. New and hot leads come first. Open a lead for everything they wrote, the live chat transcript, their calls, every contact logged and the claim history.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-work-a-lead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work a lead</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Claim</b> on a card, or <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> for the oldest hot lead nobody holds. It is yours for 15 minutes; nobody else can work on it meanwhile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>. Your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged on the lead. Each call, text, email or <b class="gd-ui">Note</b> adds another 15 minutes to your claim, up to 60 minutes from when you claimed it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Outcome</b> and choose Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won (with the booking number when there is one) or Lost (say why). Won and lost close the lead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing more to do? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark handled</b>. Done with it for now? Press <b class="gd-ui">Unclaim</b>: it goes back to the pool at once.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A claim that runs out returns the lead to the pool for everyone. One person holds at most 25 leads at a time. When a renter lead&#39;s person books and the booking is confirmed, the lead closes as Won by itself, for the Sales person on the booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-as-an-admin" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">As an Admin</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> gives a lead to a person (their claim, and the lead is assigned to them). <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> ends someone&#39;s claim.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Sales team</b> shows each person&#39;s leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week or this month, best first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> sets how long a claim holds for renter, owner and partner leads (10 to 15 minutes suggested), the most a claim can be extended to, how many leads one person may hold, and how long a lead counts as hot.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Filters narrow the list by type, source, status, age, person and your own leads; the search finds a name, phone number, email or words they wrote.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'hiring', 'chapter', 'referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage', 'Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role''s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.

## Open a role and send the apply link

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links.

1. Press **Open the role** to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); **Close the role** takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.
2. Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.
3. Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role''s questions, about five minutes.
4. **Pass mark and pay** changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.

## What happens to each application

The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.

- Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).
- Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so.
- Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.
- A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.
- Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.

## Review the applications

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Applications.

1. Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.
2. **Invite anyway** sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. **Decline** sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).
3. A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.

## Interview days

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Interview days.

1. Press **Add an interview day**: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).
2. Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate''s email and on their page.
3. Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.
4. **Turn off** stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.

## Run the calls with the rubric

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Calls.

1. Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press **Start**.
2. The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.
3. Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press **Save the rubric**. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.

## Shortlist and Hire

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Shortlist.

1. Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.
2. Open the candidate and press **Hire**. A short form opens: the **Role** (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the **Start date** and the **Pay**, filled in with the role''s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.
3. Press **Confirm: hire and start onboarding**. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do''s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email; their call slot and AI interview link close.
4. The **Onboarding** card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire''s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press **Send the agreement**. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press **Verify**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.
5. **Not hired** closes a candidate after the call without an email; **Withdrawn** is for one who no longer wants the role.

> Good to know: Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.


> Good to know: A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows "N applicants invited but no interview day is open for" the role, with **Add an interview day**. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time ("No call times are open right now"), get "New times are open" when the day is added.

## Decisions and the emails they send

The rubric''s **Decision** is Hire, Maybe, No, **Good fit for Sales instead** or No show. Recording one sends nothing.

1. **Good fit for Sales instead** refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.
2. Open **Hiring**, **Emails to send**: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.
3. **Change** a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or **Undo** it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).
4. Press **Send all decision emails**. Choose **Now**, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press **Hire** on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.

## AI interviews for the remote roles

Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. **People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: **Turn off** sends the remote roles the booking link again. **Interview settings**: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).

1. The candidate gets one email, **Start my interview**. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.
2. They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role''s rubric: experience, the role''s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role''s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Without a camera or a microphone they type, on the same clock. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.
3. When the last answer is in, the candidate is **Interviewed**. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: **Invite to a live call**, **Hire**, **Decline** or **Good fit for Sales instead**. Hiring shows "N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision".
4. Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript and the AI''s score for that rubric line. **Watch all** plays every video one after the other.
5. You decide, as after a call: the rubric''s **Decision**, then **Emails to send**. Or press **Invite to a live call**: the candidate gets the link to book a video call (they wait for an interview day like everyone else).
6. A link that expired: **New interview link** emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.

> Good to know: The AI never hires or declines anyone: nothing goes to the candidate until you send the decision emails. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings > Usage, "Hiring interviews"); when today''s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.

## Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed

- The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day''s **How** is only the default shown.
- Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with **Confirm my call** (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.
- **Calls** shows **Confirmed**, **Waiting** or **Asked 24 hours before** for each remote call, and **Cancelled: not confirmed** for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.
', 'Hiring', 'Open roles and apply links for Indeed and OnlineJobs.ph, the applications and their scores, AI interviews for the remote roles, interview days, the rubric during each call, the ranked shortlist and Hire.',
  'Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role''s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.

## Open a role and send the apply link

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links.

1. Press **Open the role** to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); **Close the role** takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.
2. Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.
3. Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role''s questions, about five minutes.
4. **Pass mark and pay** changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.

## What happens to each application

The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.

- Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).
- Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so.
- Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.
- A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.
- Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.

## Review the applications

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Applications.

1. Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.
2. **Invite anyway** sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. **Decline** sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).
3. A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.

## Interview days

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Interview days.

1. Press **Add an interview day**: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).
2. Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate''s email and on their page.
3. Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.
4. **Turn off** stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.

## Run the calls with the rubric

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Calls.

1. Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press **Start**.
2. The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.
3. Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press **Save the rubric**. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.

## Shortlist and Hire

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Shortlist.

1. Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.
2. Open the candidate and press **Hire**. A short form opens: the **Role** (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the **Start date** and the **Pay**, filled in with the role''s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.
3. Press **Confirm: hire and start onboarding**. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do''s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email; their call slot and AI interview link close.
4. The **Onboarding** card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire''s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press **Send the agreement**. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press **Verify**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.
5. **Not hired** closes a candidate after the call without an email; **Withdrawn** is for one who no longer wants the role.

> Good to know: Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.


> Good to know: A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows "N applicants invited but no interview day is open for" the role, with **Add an interview day**. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time ("No call times are open right now"), get "New times are open" when the day is added.

