er: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Without a camera or a microphone they type, on the same clock. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript and the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">You decide, as after a call: the rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>. Or press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>: the candidate gets the link to book a video call (they wait for an interview day like everyone else).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The AI never hires or declines anyone: nothing goes to the candidate until you send the decision emails. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'alerts-the-bell-and-your-phone', 'chapter', 'quick-reference', 'The bell at the top of the menu opens **Alerts**: every alert for you, newest first, with the number not yet read. The same alerts reach your phone when phone alerts are on. Nothing to set up.

## The list

1. Press the bell. **All**, **Unread** or **Urgent** narrows the list.
2. Press an alert to open its page; it is marked read. **Mark read** or **Mark all read** clears without opening.
3. **Snooze 30 min** on an urgent alert: it comes again in 30 minutes and is not passed on meanwhile.

Red dot: urgent and unread. Black dot: unread.

## What alerts you

| Group | Alerts |
| --- | --- |
| Leads | New renter lead (form, phone number box, game claim, live chat), request typed and not sent, new owner lead and unfinished application, visitor turning Hot |
| Bookings | Confirmed, going out, back, closed, no-show (urgent), cancelled, offer sent, viewed, accepted and about to expire, extension asked or paid, change asked or applied, deposit released, insurer booking with no claim number |
| Money | Payment of $500 or more, refund, deposit hold failed and card declined at pickup (urgent), owner debit failed (urgent), investor money, the 9 pm cash summary |
| Field work | Job assigned, started, finished, running late (urgent), checklist incomplete, fuel or km off at return |
| Documents | Licence to review, agreement signed, agreement not signed 2 hours before pickup (urgent), insurance proof missing 24 hours before |
| Customers | Reviews (3 stars or less urgent), complaint words in chat, texts or emails, account deletion asked (urgent), unsubscribes and STOP (in Alerts only) |
| Fleet | Tracker offline, left the zone or Ontario, speeding, driving after the return time, battery (urgent), service due (in Alerts only), car paused or unpublished |
| Owners and investors | Owner gives notice (urgent), owner banking changed (urgent), investor signed |
| System | Admin sign-in from a new device or country (urgent), many failed sign-ins (urgent), deploy finished or failed, usage over 80% and data health (in Alerts only) |
| Staff and hiring | Academy lessons, quizzes failed twice, certified; Sales late or idle in their hours; new application, AI interview scored, link expired, offer accepted |
| Wins | First booking of a car, record day or week, an owner''s first payout, the month''s totals on the 1st |
| Briefs | 8 am morning brief, 9 pm evening wrap; an urgent alert nobody opened |

Also a line for each important message sent to a renter, owner or investor (late notices and the return-time notice are urgent).

## Buttons on a phone alert

- **Call**: opens your phone''s dialer with the lead''s or renter''s number (the Quo app if it handles your calls).
- **Send offer**, **Approve** or **Decline**, **Mark picked up**: open the booking where you do it. Nothing is decided from the lock screen.
- **Snooze 30 min** on urgent alerts.

## Who gets what

- Customer service, Sales and Fleet get their function''s alerts while on duty (Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes), and what is assigned to them. Field staff get their jobs. Each gets a morning brief of their own work at 8 am.
- An urgent alert a team member did not open in 15 minutes goes to the next person on duty, then to you after another 15.
- More than 5 alerts of one kind in 10 minutes reach the phone once, as a group; each stays in the list.
- Test and verification accounts never get alerts, and a test address never makes one.

## Settings

**Alerts** > **Settings**:

1. **Phone alerts**: turn them on for this device, choose the topics, or keep a different choice on this device only.
2. **Quiet hours** (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them): normal alerts wait until they end. Urgent alerts always come.
3. **Focus mode** for 1 or 3 hours: only urgent alerts reach your phone; the rest wait in the list.
4. **Which alerts staff get**: each kind on or off, and urgent, normal or digest.

> Tip: the full table of every alert and every role is docs/alerts/matrix.md in the code.

## Alerts by email

Staff and Admin alerts that are not urgent no longer come one email each: they come together in one email at most once an hour, with everything since the last one. Urgent ones still come on their own, at most 3 an hour: a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, and the site down. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once either way. Choose under **Settings** > **My profile**, Notifications: alerts by email, **Change how often**: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.
', 'Alerts: the bell and your phone', 'Every alert for you in one list, the buttons on a phone alert, quiet hours, focus mode, and which alerts staff get.',
