select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-jobs', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Your day, in order: handovers, returns, deliveries, moves and photo shoots. Each job card has the car, the plate, the place and the time.

## Your job list

1. The menu: **My jobs**, **Cars now**, **Map** (where the cars of your jobs are now, with their trips and alerts), **My hours** and **Me** (My sales, Referrals, Profile and Academy, as a row on top). **Add a rental** and **Report a problem** are buttons at the top of My jobs. **Sign out** is top right.
2. Switch between **Today** and **Tomorrow**. Jobs are in time order.
3. The next job is the big card at the top: its time and how long until it, the car and its plate, the place with **Open in maps** and a button to call the renter, and what to put in the car. The rest of the day follows in time order.
4. A handover or a return has its own button: **Check in (pickup)** or **Check out (return)**. One tap acknowledges and starts the job and opens its photo checklist. Other jobs: press **Open the job**.
5. Moving a car that has no job? Use Vehicle moves (see below).

![](/guides/img/field-01-today-phone-b31e25fb.jpg "phone; size: 390 1530; pins: 1 91.0 15.0, 2 89.7 53.3, 3 89.7 61.4, 4 89.7 88.2")

> Tip: Need help on a job? Call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991. The link is at the bottom of My jobs.

## Open a job

1. The card shows the kind, the time, the car, the plate and colour.
2. The address, with **Open in maps** for directions, and a button to call the renter.
3. For a handover: the booking, the renter''s name and phone, the Card on File and the licence on file.
4. Press **Acknowledge** so the office knows you have it. Then press **Start** when you are with the car.

![](/guides/img/field-02-job-phone-c6780f54.jpg "phone; size: 390 1530; pins: 1 94.9 34.0, 2 94.9 44.1, 3 94.9 52.6, 4 94.9 95.8")

## Check the renter''s licence

The renter''s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and "field staff".

1. My jobs shows **Licences to check** when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under **Check the licence**.
2. Press **Review the licence**. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.
3. Look at each image and the licence reader''s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told why and sends a new one.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once.

> Tip: The renter''s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).

## Move a car

1. Under Vehicle moves, press **Start a move**. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).
2. Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press **Start the move now**.
3. When you arrive, press **End the move**, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press **End the move now**.

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. My jobs shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Cars now

**Field work** > **Cars now** shows which cars are out, coming back today and tomorrow, going out in the next 72 hours and free, with no money. The renter''s phone shows only on your own jobs.


## Call and text the renter

**Call** on a job opens the Quo app with the renter''s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; **Text** opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking. Without the Quo app, use **Use this phone** in the window that opens.

**Search:** the **Search** button at the top finds your jobs by booking number, plate or car.

## Your shifts

Jobs are given only to people on a shift that day. On **My jobs**, **Your shifts** lists the shifts you hold and the open ones: press **Take this shift** on the days you can work, or **Give this shift up** if you cannot. You can take shifts once you have passed the academy. If a day has no shifts, work due that day is done the day before or the day after; the job shows the planned day and the real time.', 'Today', 'Your shift, then one list of the day: each car and time is one card. The Add button, and helping a renter on the spot.',
  'The portal has four tabs at the bottom of the screen: **Today**, **My shifts**, **My pay** and **Training** (and **Sales** if you asked to do sales too). Today is where the work is.

## Your shift and the clock

1. At the top of **Today**: your shift, and **Clock in**. Press it when you start. The phone shares where you are at that moment only.
2. The bar shows how many of the day''s must-dos are done.
3. When you finish, press **Clock out**. Anything still open is listed: give a reason for each, then press **Clock out with these reasons**. Fleet is told, so someone can cover them.

## One list, in order

The list is built for you from the bookings and the cars:

1. **Your work**: every pickup and return of the day (deliveries and collections too) at its time, and onboarding prep Fleet gave you. Each car and time is one card.
2. **When you have time**: cars to clean (not checked clean for a week), cars needing service or not roadworthy, and cars that need listing photos.
3. Switch to **Tomorrow** to see what is planned so far.

## A card

1. The time, what it is (Pickup, Return, Delivery to the renter), the car and its plate, the renter and the booking.
2. The steps of the card, ticked as they are done: the clean check, the add-ons in the car, the pickup photos and handover.
3. One big button: the next thing to do. **Start the pickup** or **Start the return** opens the job screen, where the clean check and the add-ons come first.
4. **More** has the place with **Open in maps**, the call to the renter, and helping the renter.

> Watch out: The pickup cannot be finished until every add-on (a child seat, for example) is ticked as in the car. If the trip must go without it, ask an Admin to override on the job.

## Clean checks

Every car is checked clean before each pickup and after each return: choose **Clean** or **Needs cleaning**, take the photo and press **Save the clean check**. On a cleaning card in spare time, press **Check it clean** the same way.

## Cars needing service, and listing photos

1. On a service card, press **Give an update** (taken in, at the shop, waiting for parts, sorted) and **Send the update to Fleet**.
2. On a photo card, press **Take the listing photos**: the photo shoot opens with the angles the listing is missing.

## Onboarding prep

Fleet gives you the prep of a car joining the fleet on a day you hold a shift. Press **Open the prep**, then each item: upload what it needs (the safety certificate with its date) and press **Mark it done**. When every item is done, the owner''s onboarding checklist updates and Fleet is told.

## The Add button

The red **Add** button at the bottom right of Today:

1. **Money spent**: gas, a wash, parts, parking. The amount, the car, the booking and a photo of the receipt, then **Send to Finance**. Finance approves it and pays you back if you used your own money. No receipt yet: you get a To do until you add it.
2. **Service record**: what was done, where, the odometer, the cost and the invoice photo, then **Record the service**. The car''s maintenance resets, the expense is made on the car, and Fleet and Finance are told.
3. **Photos of a car**: a photo and a note, saved on the car.
4. **A problem with a car**: damage, a warning light, a ticket or lost property (see Report, rentals, referrals and profile).

## Help a renter on the spot

From a card''s **More**, or with **Find the booking** on Help a renter (by booking number, name or phone):

1. **Take a payment** or **Take the deposit hold**: **Show a QR for their phone** (they pay on their own phone), **Text the link**, **Email the link**, or **Use the card reader** when you have it. Never type a card number.
2. The licence: check it in person on the pickup.
3. The agreement: **They sign on my phone**, with their own finger.

> Good to know: Refunds stay with Finance and Admin.

## Check the renter''s licence

The renter''s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and "field staff".

1. My jobs shows **Licences to check** when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under **Check the licence**.
2. Press **Review the licence**. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.
3. Look at each image and the licence reader''s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told why and sends a new one.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once.

> Tip: The renter''s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. My jobs shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Move a car

1. Under Moving a car, press **Start a move**. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).
2. Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press **Start the move now**.
3. When you arrive, press **End the move**, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press **End the move now**.

## Call and text the renter

**Call** on a card opens the Quo app with the renter''s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; **Text** opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.

**Cars now** and **Map of your cars** are links at the bottom of Today.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">The portal has four tabs at the bottom of the screen: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, <b class="gd-ui">My shifts</b>, <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Training</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> if you asked to do sales too). Today is where the work is.</p><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-your-shift-and-the-clock" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your shift and the clock</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>: your shift, and <b class="gd-ui">Clock in</b>. Press it when you start. The phone shares where you are at that moment only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many of the day&#39;s must-dos are done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you finish, press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out</b>. Anything still open is listed: give a reason for each, then press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out with these reasons</b>. Fleet is told, so someone can cover them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-one-list-in-order" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One list, in order</h2><p class="gd-p">The list is built for you from the bookings and the cars:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Your work</b>: every pickup and return of the day (deliveries and collections too) at its time, and onboarding prep Fleet gave you. Each car and time is one card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">When you have time</b>: cars to clean (not checked clean for a week), cars needing service or not roadworthy, and cars that need listing photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Switch to <b class="gd-ui">Tomorrow</b> to see what is planned so far.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-a-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A card</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The time, what it is (Pickup, Return, Delivery to the renter), the car and its plate, the renter and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The steps of the card, ticked as they are done: the clean check, the add-ons in the car, the pickup photos and handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One big button: the next thing to do. <b class="gd-ui">Start the pickup</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Start the return</b> opens the job screen, where the clean check and the add-ons come first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">More</b> has the place with <b class="gd-ui">Open in maps</b>, the call to the renter, and helping the renter.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The pickup cannot be finished until every add-on (a child seat, for example) is ticked as in the car. If the trip must go without it, ask an Admin to override on the job.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-clean-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Clean checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car is checked clean before each pickup and after each return: choose <b class="gd-ui">Clean</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Needs cleaning</b>, take the photo and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the clean check</b>. On a cleaning card in spare time, press <b class="gd-ui">Check it clean</b> the same way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-cars-needing-service-and-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars needing service, and listing photos</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a service card, press <b class="gd-ui">Give an update</b> (taken in, at the shop, waiting for parts, sorted) and <b class="gd-ui">Send the update to Fleet</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On a photo card, press <b class="gd-ui">Take the listing photos</b>: the photo shoot opens with the angles the listing is missing.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-onboarding-prep" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Onboarding prep</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet gives you the prep of a car joining the fleet on a day you hold a shift. Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the prep</b>, then each item: upload what it needs (the safety certificate with its date) and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark it done</b>. When every item is done, the owner&#39;s onboarding checklist updates and Fleet is told.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-the-add-button" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Add button</h2><p class="gd-p">The red <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> button at the bottom right of Today:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money spent</b>: gas, a wash, parts, parking. The amount, the car, the booking and a photo of the receipt, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to Finance</b>. Finance approves it and pays you back if you used your own money. No receipt yet: you get a To do until you add it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Service record</b>: what was done, where, the odometer, the cost and the invoice photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Record the service</b>. The car&#39;s maintenance resets, the expense is made on the car, and Fleet and Finance are told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photos of a car</b>: a photo and a note, saved on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A problem with a car</b>: damage, a warning light, a ticket or lost property (see Report, rentals, referrals and profile).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-help-a-renter-on-the-spot" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Help a renter on the spot</h2><p class="gd-p">From a card&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">More</b>, or with <b class="gd-ui">Find the booking</b> on Help a renter (by booking number, name or phone):</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Take a payment</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take the deposit hold</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Show a QR for their phone</b> (they pay on their own phone), <b class="gd-ui">Text the link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the link</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Use the card reader</b> when you have it. Never type a card number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The licence: check it in person on the pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement: <b class="gd-ui">They sign on my phone</b>, with their own finger.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Refunds stay with Finance and Admin.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-check-the-renter-s-licence" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check the renter&#39;s licence</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and &quot;field staff&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">My jobs shows <b class="gd-ui">Licences to check</b> when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under <b class="gd-ui">Check the licence</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b>. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Look at each image and the licence reader&#39;s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>. The renter is told why and sends a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter&#39;s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-documents-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents to sign</h2><p class="gd-p">Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">My jobs shows &quot;You have a document to sign&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-move-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Move a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Moving a car, press <b class="gd-ui">Start a move</b>. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press <b class="gd-ui">Start the move now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you arrive, press <b class="gd-ui">End the move</b>, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press <b class="gd-ui">End the move now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-call-and-text-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and text the renter</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a card opens the Quo app with the renter&#39;s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Map of your cars</b> are links at the bottom of Today.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'chapter', 'photo-shoots', 'Clock in when you start and out when you finish. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved, and you get a pay statement for each pay.

## Clock in and out

1. Open **My hours**. When you start work, add a note if you like (for example where you start) and press **Clock in**.
2. The big clock shows how long you have been on. The jobs you finish while clocked in are listed under it.
3. When you finish, press **Clock out**. Add a note if you like. Your shift is saved with the time of each press.
4. Under **Recent shifts** you see the last three weeks, each with its jobs. **This pay period so far** shows your hours and what they come to at your rate.

> Watch out: Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? You cannot change it yourself. Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log. A shift left running more than 16 hours has to be fixed by Fleet or an Admin.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under **Pay statements** on **My hours**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.', 'My shifts and My pay', 'Claim, give up and swap shifts, what you did on each, your hours, pay statements and pay details.',
  'Jobs go only to people on a shift. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Press **Claim this shift**. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the work planned so far. It updates as bookings come in.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.
',
